Add an all-in-one inventory for the deployer.

Kolla Ansible can be run from a container on the host it deploys to,
such as the kolla-ansible image built by Kolla. The container then
reaches its own host through the community.docker.nsenter connection
plugin, with no SSH. The all-in-one inventory cannot be used for that
with only its connection changed, because it names the deploy host
localhost.

Some tasks run with delegate_to: localhost and connection: local, using
paths that exist only where Ansible runs. Keystone's fernet cron
generator, for example, runs a script from its role directory with
ansible_playbook_python. An inventory host named localhost replaces
Ansible's implicit one, and a host's ansible_connection takes precedence
over a task's connection keyword, so those tasks would run on the host
and fail.

This change adds all-in-one-deployer beside all-in-one. It differs only
in that:

* the deploy host is named kolla, so that every use of localhost stays
  in the container;
* ansible_connection=community.docker.nsenter in [all:vars] replaces
  ansible_connection=local on each host line; and
* ansible_remote_tmp is an absolute path. The nsenter plugin assumes
  that remote_user is root, and passes the container's environment,
  including HOME, to commands on the host, so the default
  ~/.ansible/tmp names a directory in the container's HOME, which the
  host does not have.

Neither all-in-one nor this inventory pins ansible_python_interpreter,
so interpreter discovery on the host is unchanged.

